{"slug":"falling-wedge-breakout","name":"Falling wedge breakout","status":"rejected","created_at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.568386Z","version":1,"frozen":true,"implementation":"wedge-breakout","runs":2,"trials":2,"deflated_sharpe":1.4703362292145528e-06,"asset_class":"crypto","sections":{"hypothesis":"Hypothesis","rationale":"Why the edge should exist","rules":"Rules in plain English","falsification":"What would prove it wrong","parameters":"Parameters and allowed ranges","costs":"Expected turnover against costs"},"notes":[{"version":1,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.568386Z","sections":{"hypothesis":"A breakout above a falling wedge (falling highs and falling lows that converge) reaches 3R more often than both its cost-adjusted break-even rate and a breakout of a falling line without the converging lower line.","rationale":"Chart-pattern lore (e.g. Bulkowski) calls the falling wedge a bullish reversal. A plausible mechanism is volatility contraction: shrinking swings mean sellers are exhausting, and contraction tends to be followed by expansion. Weak point: pattern studies are mostly hand-labelled after the fact, and wedges are rare once the definition leaves no room for judgement.","rules":"Shared definitions: 4h bars; swing high/low = a bar's high (low) beats the 3 bars before it and isn't beaten by the 3 bars after it, known only 3 bars later; ATR = 14-bar average true range at the signal bar. Lines and levels use only swings known at the signal bar. Buy at the next open; risk 1% per trade (spot, no leverage); one position at a time. Upper line: through the two most recent known swing highs, the later one lower. Lower line: through the two most recent known swing lows, the later one lower. Wedge: both lines fall, and the gap between them at the latest swing is at most 60% of the gap at the earliest of the four swings (converging). Breakout: a close more than 0.5 ATR above the projected upper line. A close below the projected lower line first spends the wedge. One entry per wedge. That close is the signal. Stop: the latest swing low. Target: 3R.","falsification":"BTCUSDT and ETHUSDT 4h, 2020-01 to 2025-10 (before the holdout), default parameters, run once. Reject if, pooled across both markets: net expectancy after costs is 0R or below; or P(expectancy > 0) is under 90%; or fewer than 50 trades; or it doesn't beat the falling trendline breakout (the note above) on the same data: convergence is the claimed edge, so the wedge must add something over the line alone.","parameters":"swing_bars 3 (2-5); converge_pct 60 (40-80); breakout_atr_pct 50 (25-100); target_r 3 (2-4). Comparison: trendline-breakout with swing_bars 3, breakout_atr_pct 50, target_r 3. Only the defaults are pre-registered.","costs":"Stops at the latest swing low, often 4-8% on 4h, so about 0.03-0.06R per round trip. The main risk is too few trades: strict wedges may give well under 50 across both markets, in which case the note's own rule rejects it as untestable."},"implementation":"wedge-breakout","frozen_at":"2026-11-11T13:05:40.336107Z","change_reason":null}],"history":[{"status":"idea","at":"2026-11-05T03:28:30.568386Z","reason":"Created"},{"status":"specified","at":"2026-11-11T13:05:40.336130Z","reason":"v1 frozen"},{"status":"backtested","at":"2026-11-11T13:05:43.208984Z","reason":"first run on v1"},{"status":"rejected","at":"2026-11-14T08:43:25.508955Z","reason":"Tested 2026-11-05 on BTC and ETH 4h: +0.17R a trade but not convincing (P(> 0) 86% against the 90% the note required). Recorded as drop; closed in the 2026-11-14 clean-out."}],"trial_log":[{"id":"20261111-130543-90be6f","created_at":"2026-11-11T13:05:43.202736Z","strategy":"wedge-breakout","strategy_kind":"research","style":"brackets","engine":"event","params":{"swing_bars":3,"converge_pct":60,"breakout_atr_pct":50,"target_r":3},"research":{"slug":"falling-wedge-breakout","version":1},"strategy_name":"falling wedge breakout 3R BTCUSDT","symbol":"BTCUSDT","benchmark_symbol":null,"universe_coins":